{
 "name": "AstriaNet PL16803 (learned from ASTRIANet frames)",
 "description": "Raw 16-bit frames of the FLI ProLine PL16803 (4096 x 4096 9 um pixels, unfiltered) at the AstriaNet node at New Mexico Skies, 1.55 arcsec/px, tracking satellites so the stars trail. Learned by skytwin-calibrate learn from 159 frames of two nights (Starlink-1422, 0.1 s; NAVSTAR 48, 3 s). The zeropoint is above the atmosphere for an assumed 0.2 mag/airmass (not measurable here: the 3 s frames all sit near airmass 1.15): give the scene's ground site extinction_mag_per_airmass 0.2.",
